Use the `@variant` directive with the breakpoint name (for example `md`) inside your CSS, and set the variable in that block. The docs show it only with `dark`, not with a breakpoint, so the `md` example below is my extrapolation.

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;

  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

- **`@variant` directive:** `src/docs/functions-and-directives.mdx`, "@variant" (lines 78–96). `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Using variants" (around line 301), covers the same directive.
- **Which breakpoints exist:** the `--breakpoint-*` theme variables define the breakpoint variants (`src/docs/theme.mdx`, "Relationship to variants", lines 103–127). A custom `--breakpoint-3xl` gives you `3xl`, so `@variant 3xl { … }` should work the same way.
- **Utility alternative:** you can also set the variable in the markup with a prefixed utility, for example `md:[--my-var:2rem]`. I didn't find that form in the docs I searched.

